<section class="about-story-section" id="about-us" aria-label="About Graffeine Tales Story">
      
      <!-- Subtle Artistic Doodle / Watermark Background -->
      <div class="story-watermark-doodle" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 700" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <path d="M120 480 C 220 320, 340 520, 500 360 C 660 200, 780 440, 920 280" stroke="#E9DFC2" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 8" stroke-opacity="0.06"/>
          <path d="M180 180 C 260 280, 420 160, 520 290 C 620 420, 760 310, 860 420" stroke="#C6B58E" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-opacity="0.05"/>
          <circle cx="500" cy="350" r="180" stroke="#E9DFC2" stroke-width="1" stroke-opacity="0.04"/>
          <circle cx="500" cy="350" r="260" stroke="#927B53" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="6 12" stroke-opacity="0.05"/>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="container story-container">
        
        <!-- Heading & Subheading -->
        <h2 class="story-section-title">The Story Behind Graffeine Tales</h2>
        <p class="story-subheading">Born from events. Brewed with coffee. Made with art.</p>

        <!-- Kinetic Scroll-Triggered Progressive Text Highlight Block -->
        <div class="story-narrative-wrap" id="story-narrative-wrap">
          <p class="story-lead story-split-text" id="story-lead-text">
            <em>It started with events. Then came design. And eventually, design became something you could hold.</em>
          </p>

          <p class="story-body story-split-text">
            My journey began in event planning, amidst tight deadlines, endless checklists, and the beautiful chaos of bringing ideas to life. Somewhere along the way, I found myself drawn to the art of designing experiences and creating moments worth remembering.
          </p>

          <p class="story-body story-split-text">
            The days were hectic, the coffee was endless, and creativity kept brewing. What began as event planning slowly evolved into event design, graphic design, and a desire to create something more personal.
          </p>

          <p class="story-body story-split-text">
            I wanted my designs to live beyond screens and event spaces — to become things people could hold, gift, use, and cherish.
          </p>

          <p class="story-body story-split-text">
            And so, <em>Graffeine Tales</em> was born: a blend of graphics and caffeine, fuelled by a love for art, handmade details, and the little things that bring joy.
          </p>

          <p class="story-body story-split-text">
            Today, from illustrated stationery and personalised gifts to thread art and handmade keepsakes, every creation is a mix of thoughtful design and a little creative magic.
          </p>

        </div>

        <!-- Call-to-Action (Single Read More Button — Redirects to About Page) -->
        <div class="story-cta-wrap">
          <a href="about.html" class="story-read-more-btn" aria-label="Read the full story behind Graffeine Tales">
            <span>Read More</span>
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line>
              <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"></polyline>
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Our Story & Atelier Philosophy",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Our Story & Atelier Philosophy"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
